Pre-existing, unrelated to NEARS-2730's diff (confirmed via git blame: verification_screen.dart:521 dates to commit 432fb55d61, 2026-06-10, last touched by NEARS-1746 on 2026-08-31 — NOT this ticket, which only touched verification_repository.dart).

Repro (artificial, edge-case): on the verification screen, tap Verify with a wrong OTP, then immediately navigate Back (Android back key) before the verify_token response returns. When the response lands after the screen has been popped/disposed, VerificationScreenState._navigatePostVerify's `verifyTokenFailed` case calls `errorController.add(ErrorAnimationType.shake)` BEFORE the `if (!mounted) return;` guard (verification_screen.dart:521, guard is at line ~535) — so a disposed StreamController still receives .add(), throwing:

